Ladybird wakes a stopped event page only for an event its last run
added a listener for, and only such an event counts as its activity.
Chromium keeps a record of the same lazy listeners, which EventRouter::
AddLazyEventListenerImpl() stores, and starts a lazy background context
only for an event that has one. Gecko primes the persistent listeners
that an event page registered in its last run (with ExtensionCommon’s
primeListener()), and only those start it. And WebKit’s
WebExtensionContext::wakeUpBackgroundContentIfNecessaryToFireEvents()
checks the event types that the background content registered before
it starts the page at all.
